{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>On the word of two witnesses</b> etc. Since it is stated above 'and it is told to you and you hear,' it writes here: even so, he shall not be put to death except <b>on the word of two witnesses or three witnesses.</b>" "<b>[On the word of two witnesses or three</b> this and not less than this, it teaches.]" "<b>He shall be put to death, the dead one.</b> Who is destined to die — as we find regarding Jacob, Joseph, and Moses: 'here I am dying.'" "<b>On the word of one witness.</b> And if you ask: what does this teach us? We already know that even in monetary matters one witness is not believed — all the more so in capital cases! One may answer: the punishment in capital cases is severe [for witnesses], and one might have said that one witness is believed — therefore it teaches us otherwise."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:11.035012590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}